# 43. Security Requirements

- repository credentials must never appear in prompts;
- API tokens must remain server-side;
- agents must operate in isolated workspaces;
- destructive commands should be blocked;
- logs should redact credentials;
- Jira authorization must respect existing user/service permissions;
- pull requests require human approval.

---

# 44. Product Differentiation

The product should not be pitched as:

> AI that reads Jira tickets and writes code.

That capability already exists in several developer-agent products.

The product should instead be pitched as:

> AI that systematically investigates competing explanations for a bug and proves which fix addresses the actual failure.

The meaningful differentiators are:

### Parallel hypotheses

Multiple root causes are explored simultaneously.

### Evidence-based selection

The winner is chosen using execution evidence.

### Regression proof

The fix must demonstrate:

```text
FAIL before
PASS after
```

### Alternative-hypothesis rejection

Users see what else was investigated.

### Human-understandable diagnosis

The output is a debugging report, not merely a diff.

